<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila ficusphila longitudinal sex-comb Turing wavelength at 2.1 µm — MorphoEval overall 88.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the Schnakenberg–Turing core (Pearson r = 0.99999994 on σ(k), RMSE = 5.2e-4, λ_c = 2.072 µm) and adds the four pass-1 remediation analyses. D_u swept from 0.55× to 2.20× gives a strictly increasing λ (endpoint ratio 2.0). The equal-diffusion run drops the field std to 0.018 of the seed. The gallery plate mask has coherency 0.8279, foreground fraction 0.3646 and circularity 0.0683, against 0.9494, 0.5381 and 0.0118 on the simulated frame. Luminance KS = 0.1879. The radial-FFT centroid of the field is 1.9175 µm, not a copy of 2.072. GIF remains 16 frames at 800×600; CV similarity to the plate is 81.9. Overall 88.8/100 (faithfulness 88.4, reproducibility 89.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_ficusphila_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 498641 B, 1632×984 px, artifact_sha256 b9fa47b593f847ad45a8f00fa2dba0c2a8477fba17b70222c1f04e1142976810 (sha256 b9fa47b593f847ad45a8f00fa2dba0c2a8477fba17b70222c1f04e1142976810), spec_fingerprint c6f261396b638d86a346006a062997a1c76d65fe1cbe8f6278c90ec0b2a806df. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c6f261396b638d86a346006a062997a1c76d65fe1cbe8f6278c90ec0b2a806df; artifact_sha256: b9fa47b593f847ad45a8f00fa2dba0c2a8477fba17b70222c1f04e1142976810; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_ficusphila_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_ficusphila_specimen.jpg=8a0ea6252701fd69..., datasets/drosophila_ficusphila_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_ficusphila_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=bb3981fcb66333ba..., datasets/drosophila_ficusphila_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=26d1e013287e2844...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952): instability at a finite critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg (1979): kinetics R_u = a - u + u^2 v, R_v = b - u^2 v. | Tanaka, Barmina & Kopp (2009): longitudinal sex combs form by rotation or by bristles born longitudinal. | Tanaka et al. (2011) and Kopp (2011): sex combs are a doublesex/Scr innovation.; reconstructed_in_script: λ_c = 2.072 µm (2.072e-6 m, log10 = -5.684) is the assigned detail tier, obtained by setting D_u at r = 20. | At 0 Ma, density 2/3 for D. eugracilis and 1/2 for D. grimshawi give λ = 3.108 µm and 4.144 µm. | Nine-point D_u sweep, equal-diffusion integration, mask coherency and the KS statistic are script measurements.; transfer_boundary: No cited paper measures a 2.072 µm sex-comb ridge or gives these Schnakenberg numbers. | The chronoseries is a project order of extant species, not a stratigraphic sequence.; does_not_claim: That the gallery plate is an SEM of a tooth. | That the power-weighted FFT centroid (1.9175 µm) is the analytic λ_c (2.072 µm). | That a second assessor scored this pass.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R1 resolved: parameter_sweep uses nine D_u factors and the comparison figure draws λ(D_u).",
        "remediation needed: R2 resolved: ablation_equal_diffusion integrates 700 steps at D_u = D_v; std ratio 0.018.",
        "remediation needed: R3 resolved: border-contrast mask reports coherency, foreground fraction and circularity on the plate and on the simulated frame.",
        "remediation needed: R4 resolved: KS statistic 0.1879, fine-grid Pearson r above 0.98, FFT centroid 1.9175 µm versus analytic 2.072 µm.",
        "remediation needed: R5 open: still a single assessor (Grok 4.7). A second provider was not available in this run." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.88e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila ficusphila longitudinal sex-comb Turing wavelength at 2.1 µm — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Nine D_u factors from 0.55 to 2.20 at fixed Jacobian and r = 20. λ_c is strictly increasing, and the endpoint ratio is 2.0, which is sqrt(2.20/0.55). The chronospecies bars remain the biological reading of that knob: shorter λ, more ridges, on the packed ficusphila comb than on eugracilis or grimshawi at 0 Ma." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

